  "how": "Submit runs 10 hidden tests. Each answer must equal the expected value.",
  "solution": "#include <vector>\n\nstd::vector<long long> range_sums(std::vector<int> nums, std::vector<std::vector<int>> queries) {\n    std::vector<long long> prefix(nums.size() + 1, 0);\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < nums.size(); ++i) prefix[i + 1] = prefix[i] + nums[i];\n    std::vector<long long> out;\n    for (const auto& q : queries) out.push_back(prefix[q[1] + 1] - prefix[q[0]]);\n    return out;\n}\n",
  "notes": [
    "`prefix[i]` holds the sum of the first `i` numbers, so `prefix[0]` is 0.",
    "The range from `l` to `r` is `prefix[r + 1] - prefix[l]`.",
    "One pass to build the table and one per query, so the work is $O(n + q)$."
  ]
}
